  "info": {
    "title": "Two-echelon supply chain (library assets)",
    "category": "Supply chain",
    "description": "A two-echelon supply chain built entirely from the Supply chain and inventory library: customers draw from a store on an (s, S) policy with lost sales, the store's replenishment orders are demand at a central warehouse that backorders, and the central warehouse buys from a capacitated supplier. Each echelon's lead time is the next one's queueing outcome, not a number. Base unit days.",
    "author": "Naga",
    "notes": "Total Cost is the holding cost of both echelons. Compare policies with the scenarios: they move the store's reorder point and order-up-to level, paired over common random numbers, on fill rate and inventory cost."
